  'steps.m.displacement.title': 'Displacement method (kinematic unknowns)',
  'steps.m.displacement.help': 'The displacement method as it is solved in class. It counts the kinematic indeterminacy, locks every joint (state 0) and releases one unknown at a time (states 1…n) with the stiffnesses 4EI/L, 2EI/L, 6EI/L², 12EI/L³ and 3EI/L. With the coefficients k_ij and the load terms it builds K·D = −R⁰, solves it and superposes the states. It takes hinges, two-force members, springs, settlements and temperature, and you choose whether members are axially rigid or have axial stiffness.',
